// 2. Warm start: sample 5 distinct random valid archs; query val_acc.
// 3. for each remaining epoch:
//    a. z-normalize observed val accs; fit ensemble of 7 _TinyMLP (hidden 64, 300 epochs, lr 1e-2, weight_decay 1e-3).
//    b. predict $\mu, \sigma$ for ALL valid archs; denormalize.
//    c. $\beta = (1-p)$ where $p$ is fraction of post-warmup budget used.
//    d. score = $\mu + \beta\,\sigma$; mask seen.
//    e. query argmax score.
// 4. return best-seen arch.

// 1. Warm-start: 10 distinct random archs.
// 2. Per step until last 4: fit ensemble of 5 _TinyMLP (200 epochs, lr 1e-2).
// 3. Build pool of 500 unseen candidates: each candidate is a mutation of a top-5 arch with prob $0.3+0.5\,p$, else random.
// 4. Predict $\mu, \sigma$; $\sigma\leftarrow\max(\sigma, 10^{-8})$; $\mu_{\text{best}}=\max$ observed.
// 5. $z=(\mu-\mu_{\text{best}})/\sigma$; $\mathrm{EI}=\sigma(z\Phi(z)+\phi(z))$; score = $\mathrm{EI}+0.05(1-p)\sigma$.
// 6. Query argmax.
// 7. Final 4 steps: greedy walk over unseen 1-edit neighbors of current best.
// 8. Return best-seen.

// 1. Pre-enumerate all valid archs and their path encodings.
